  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incoming mission from Bangladesh &#x2013; Seed sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The growth of the horticultural sector in Bangladesh depends on the availability of good quality seeds of high yielding varieties. However, one of the key issues in the horticultural seed supply in Bangladesh is the limited availability of quality seeds of improved varieties and a lack of conducive, regulatory framework for seed development and production.One of the aims of the combi-track &quot;Sustainable horticulture&quot; in Bangladesh is to increase access to more sustainable and efficient seeds and improve the enabling environment for horticultural inputs.Therefore, a trade mission to the Netherlands with Bangladeshi companies and policy officers will be organised, to reach the following goals:&#x2022;	Stimulate Business-to-Business (B2B) cooperation between Dutch and Bangladeshi small- and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) by networking and matchmaking to enhance food and nutritional security in Bangladesh, by ensuring the consistent supply of quality and climate-resilient seeds. &#x2022;	Transfer of knowledge and skills and strengthening Government-to-Government (G2G) and Business-to-Business (B2B) collaboration between Bangladesh and the Netherlands, to contribute to a better enabling environment in the seed sector in Bangladesh.</narrative>
  </description>
